  "market": [
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=122713",
      "title": "What Europe’s new green rules mean for printers and publishers",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/what-europes-new-green-rules-mean-for-printers-and-publishers/",
      "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:42:12 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>From paper sourcing and transport packaging to environmental claims, new EU legislation is extending compliance responsibilities across the printing and publishing value chain. Companies must now pay closer attention to their obligations across different European markets.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/what-europes-new-green-rules-mean-for-printers-and-publishers/\">What Europe&#8217;s new green rules mean for printers and publishers</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=122633",
      "title": "Amplify, normalise – or silence? How to effectively cover populism, by the playbook",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/amplify-normalise-or-silence-how-to-effectively-cover-populism-by-the-playbook/",
      "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:53:06 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Ten years of research by Ayala Panievsky reveals an uncomfortable truth: traditional journalistic norms like objectivity and balance are frequently weaponised by populist leaders. She's distilled lived experience and empirical insights into a comprehensive guide offering actionable solidarity tactics. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/amplify-normalise-or-silence-how-to-effectively-cover-populism-by-the-playbook/\">Amplify, normalise – or silence? How to effectively cover populism, by the playbook</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=122695",
      "title": "User needs in the age of agents",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/user-needs-in-the-age-of-agents/",
      "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:47:38 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Ezra Eeman and Dmitry Shishkin took the Digital Media Europe stage last week to explain and explore how user needs are changing and emerging in a media landscape increasingly populated with AI agents. Here, they share insights and visions from their “Beyond ‘Update Me’: Designing Journalism for People and Machines” session. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/user-needs-in-the-age-of-agents/\">User needs in the age of agents</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
